v 3
d gpolish: publication-style Stata graphs, with an optional matplotlib final render
d
d gpolish edits a graph after it is drawn: direct end-of-line labels with
d collision avoidance, automatically placed callouts and point labels,
d shaded finding boxes, braces, arrows, and legend text coloured like its keys.  The result is still a
d Stata graph.  The scheme pypolish sets matching defaults.
d
d gr2mpl redraws a Stata graph held in memory with matplotlib (twoway,
d graph bar/box/dot, by(), combine, marginsplot) and carries gpolish edits
d across.  It needs Python with matplotlib and numpy; gpolish itself does not.
d
d Start with: help gpolish
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261118
